[b]Speculative Markets 1.2.2[/b]

[list]
[*]Booms land softer. A boom whose price stays at or above where it began can only end in a Correction. A Bust needs the price to fall below where the boom began, and a Collapse needs it to fall well below. Building mines and factories to meet real demand is no longer punished as a Collapse. The boom ending tooltips say so.
[*]Contest moves now play out over months. Bear Raid and Shore Up cost a share of their price each month, and their pushes on the contest bar arrive a month at a time. Lure Capital's debt also arrives a month at a time, so it no longer sets off a panic the moment it is taken.
[*]If the treasury cannot pay a month of a Bear Raid or Shore Up, the move ends. An unpaid Bear Raid gives back the rest of its hit on the target, so a rival can no longer be hurt without paying for it.
[*]A Lure ends if a panic begins, and its push is lost. Its tooltip warns when its debt would lift the panic line above your Market Confidence.
[*]A short notice tells you when one of your campaigns ends early.
[*]Bank rescues no longer make banks laxer. A panic still sobers rescued banks, by half as much as banks left to fail. Bad Debts now make banks stricter each month, twice as fast under Tight credit. Before, they held Lending Standards still.
[*]The Exchange tab's world list shows every Provincial market, best first. Each tier can be folded away.
[*]The Exchange Score and Trust headings show this month's change, as Market Confidence does.
[*]The contest tooltip shows how far the bar moved this month and what moved it: the score lead, blue chips, and each side's pushes.
[*]Pinned goods in the outliner show the good's Investor Interest and the ending its boom would reach.
[*]A good's throughput from Investor Interest, the Encourage and Restrain levers and a recent company crash now sits on its buildings as one modifier. Before, each was a country modifier, and they crowded the country's modifier list. The amounts are the same.
[/list]

[b]Balance[/b]
[list]
[*]High leverage lifts the confidence a panic starts at by up to 55 points (was 50).
[*]Bad Debts fade by 0.35 points a month (was 0.3). The AI's longest lending freezes are shorter.
[*]Buying up the banks' bad loans clears 25% of the remaining Bad Debts (was 30%).
[*]A country's income counts as at least 0.9% of its GDP a month when working out leverage (was 1%).
[*]Lure Capital's debt arrives over 12 months, half a month of the investment pool each month (was all 6 months at once).
[/list]

Campaigns started before 1.2.2 are paid in full and run as they were.
